<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"RX_FREQ_BAND_1_HELP">RX FREQ BAND 1 H=
ELP</span></h3>
<pre>
The Rx Frequency Band 1 can be toggled through all currently available
frequency bands. Valid toggle choices are:  UHF Range 0, UHF Range 1, UHF R=
ange 2,
UHF Range 3, UHF Range 4, VHF Range 1, VHF Range 2, 800 MHz, 900 MHz,
and NONE.
=20
UHF Range 0 is only available for Conventional and IntelliRepeater 3.0/3.5/=
4.1 Quantar stations.
=20
If changed, the selected RX FREQ BAND 1 may be verified with the station
by pressing the Validate Configuration button. Any mismatch with the statio=
n
configuration will be reported by the RSS.
=20
If the choice of receiver is NONE (for Conventional Stations both=20
Rx Frequency Band must be set to NONE), the station will function as a tran=
smit
only station provided that a valid Tx Freq Band is selected. This
choice is typically used for paging station applications.
 </pre>
