<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"BATTERY_HELP">BATTERY HELP</span></h3=
>
<pre>
For Quantar stations or satellite receivers, the BATTERY field=20
may be toggled between NONE, LEAD ACID LINEAR, LEAD ACID=20
NONLINEAR, and NICAD. The station or receiver will utilize the=20
battery type selected to allow the power supplies' battery=20
charging circuitry to select the best charging rate for the type=20
of battery the system is using.=20

Setting the battery type to NONE will DISABLE the charging=20
circuitry, but it does not affect the battery revert or low=20
battery disconnect, which are built in the power supply=20
hardware.  Select NONE for the battery type if the batteries to be=20
used are charged from an external battery charger.=20

The BATTERY field also determines the amount of time the station will=20
"equalize" the batteries. In order to maintain proper charge and=20
capacity, some batteries require periodic equalization. During this=20
process, the charging voltage from the power supply is increased=20
slightly to ensure that the individual cells of the battery are=20
charged to a uniform level.=20

When equalization is turned on, the station will start and maintain a=20
timer and will turn equalization off when the timer expires.  The=20
battery types and their equalization times are as follows:=20

None                 : Not Equalized=20
Lead Acid Non-Linear&nbsp;: Not Equalized=20
Lead Acid Linear     : 72 Hours=20
NICAD                : 48 Hours=20

Equalization will automatically start when AC power is restored to a=20
station.  During this period, if the AC power is lost the station=20
will revert to battery power. When the AC power is restored the=20
equalization will continue with the remaining timer value.  This=20
automatic equalization feature can be manually disabled from the=20
Service:Alignment:Battery Equalization screen.  This screen also allows=20
the equalization process to be manually started, as long as the BATTERY=20
type supports equalization.=20

When a battery is selected, the station  will set the=20
station's transmit output power utilizing the number=20
programmed in the Battery Backup field, on the Channel=20
Information Screen, whenever AC power is lost.=20

For Quantro stations, the BATTERY field may be toggled=20
between NONE and INSTALLED.  The Quantro station utilizes=20
this field for selecting the station's transmit output power=20
from the Battery Backup field whenever AC power is lost.=20

This field does NOT control the battery charging circuitry.=20
Battery charging on a Quantro station is manually set on the=20
power supply itself.=20

For high power Quantar stations, the station will maintain the=20
PA output power as defined in this field as long as the DC input=20
voltage is above 27.5 Volts.  When the DC voltage drops below=20
27.5 Volts,  the output power will be derated based upon the input=20
DC voltage level, until that level drops to 21 Volts.  At that point,=20
the output power will be shut down to protect the batteries.=20

For low power Quantar stations, the station will maintain the PA output=20
power as defined in this field as long as the DC input voltage is above=20
13.8 Volts.  When the DC voltage drops below 13.8 Volts, the output=20
power will be derated based upon the input DC voltage level, until that=20
level drops to 10.5 Volts.  At that point, the output power will be shut=20
down to protect the batteries.=20
</pre>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"SYSTEM_TYPE_HELP">SYSTEM TYPE HELP</s=
pan></h3>
<pre>
The System Type may be toggled between CONVENTIONAL, TRUNKING (6809
SmartZone), TRUNKING (6809 SMARTNET), INTELLIREPEATER 2.0.3/2.7E,
INTELLIREPEATER 3.0/3.5, DSSIII and QUANTAR DATA BASE STATION.

CONVENTIONAL operation implies either a Base or Conventional Repeater
operation. IntelliRepeater implies a Trunked, system operation.

NOTE: If the station is configured as a 'local channel' (Console and/or
Interconnect interface) in a 6809-SmartZone system this field must be
set to 6809-Smartnet.

If changed, the selected SYSTEM TYPE may be verified with the
station by pressing the Validate Configuration Button. Any mismatch with th=
e
hardware configuration will be reported by the RSS.

WARNING: When the SYSTEM TYPE is changed, the resulting codeplug will
contain one channel, and any other channel information will be lost.
Other fields throughout the RSS, which are dependent on the SYSTEM TYPE,
may be changed.

NOTE: When changing the Station Type or System Type, the DIGITAL
      IDLE LINK CHECK field on the Wireline Configuration screen,
      Page 2, gets set to a default.

      Before downloading the codeplug, make sure that the field is
      set as needed by the system configuration.
</pre>
